-- T-263 -- the worker step types and `completed_with_failures`. Drawn in
-- docs/build/data-model.md before it was written; generated by drizzle-kit
-- against the re-synced snapshot (T-344) and read before being applied.
--
-- THE ONLY MIGRATION THE WORKER WAVE NEEDS. A worker invocation is a Step in
-- the existing append-only tree and, where it delegates, a child Run --
-- parent_run_id / parent_step_id / child_run_id already carry that and the
-- retrieve leaf already does exactly this. Model id, usage, cost, egress facts,
-- source set and rail outcomes are all already columns on the Step row. What
-- was missing was only the vocabulary for what KIND of step a worker
-- invocation is.
--
-- All seven worker types land at once, including the three whose workers are
-- beyond V1 (`authority_lookup`, `web_research`, `verifier`). The audit store
-- is append-only and cannot be restructured later -- ADR-0028 section 3's
-- reasoning for fixing the recursive shape from the first migration, applied to
-- the type: fixing the step vocabulary once is cheaper and safer than widening
-- an enum on a live audit table once per worker.
--
-- `completed_with_failures` is the state a MULTI-WORKER plan needs and a
-- four-step chain never did. The chain fails hard, which is right when every
-- step feeds the next; once a plan fans out, one failed branch beside a
-- completed one is neither `completed` nor `failed`, and reporting it as either
-- is a lie about what the user is holding. The semantics are T-268; this is the
-- vocabulary they are written in.
--
-- ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE runs inside the migration's transaction safely
-- because nothing here USES a new value; the first rows carrying them are
-- written by T-265 onward (migration 0054's precedent).

ALTER TYPE "public"."run_state" ADD VALUE 'completed_with_failures';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."step_type" ADD VALUE 'corpus_retrieval';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."step_type" ADD VALUE 'authority_lookup';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."step_type" ADD VALUE 'web_research';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."step_type" ADD VALUE 'extractor';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."step_type" ADD VALUE 'workflow_runner';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."step_type" ADD VALUE 'document_builder';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TYPE "public"."step_type" ADD VALUE 'verifier';